-- One system per city, enforced.
--
-- The catalogue is regenerated by scripts/verify-systems.mjs, which derives a
-- slug from the registry's System ID. Those ids are not stable across runs --
-- Chicago arrived as 'chi' when it was typed by hand and as 'lyft-chi' from
-- the registry -- so keying the upsert on slug would quietly create a second
-- Chicago with no stations and leave every existing trip pointing at the
-- first. The city is what the app looks a system up by, so the city is what
-- has to be unique, and a regenerated catalogue updates the row that is
-- already there rather than racing it.
create unique index bike_systems_one_per_city
  on public.bike_systems (lower(city));
